    "csv.guide.transactions.rules": {
      "comment": "v1.5 pending English; structured CSV explanatory copy; protocol field names must stay byte-exact",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Date: Required date the transaction occurred.\nType: Must be Income or Expense with exact capitalization. Amount is the original-currency amount. Only import income and expenses that actually occurred. Do not infer income or expenses from transfers, balances, starting assets, deposit or loan principal, or rule definitions.\nFor negative amounts and refunds, determine the correct income/expense direction from the original evidence, then enter a positive amount. Do not simply take the absolute value."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Date：交易发生日期，必填。\nType：仅 Income（收入）或 Expense（支出），大小写一致。Amount为原币金额。仅导入已经发生的收入或支出；转账、余额、期初资产、存贷款本金和规则定义不能猜作收支。\n负数、退款必须根据原始证据明确收支方向，再填写正数；不能直接取绝对值。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "csv.template.instructions": {
      "comment": "v1.5 pending English; structured CSV explanatory copy; protocol field names must stay byte-exact",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For AI: This is a blank FinTrack \"%@\" CSV template (v1).\nThe user only needs to supply the original ledger and this file, without separate instructions. The source ledger may be Excel, CSV, PDF, photographs, scans, text, or other readable material. Identify itemized records first; if the source cannot be read or is ambiguous, ask the user.\nProcess only \"%@\". Do not include any of the other three data types. List other types and uncertain data separately for review; do not reclassify them as the selected type without authorization.\nCurrent ledger base currency: %@. Never change the base currency yourself or guess currencies or historical exchange rates.\n\nFile Structure\nThe first CSV record begins with #FinTrackTemplate and stores the version, data type, and base currency. The second record begins with #AIInstructions; its second cell contains these instructions. Neither record is financial data, a header, a transaction, or a rule. The third record is the actual header below:\n%@\nRetain every column in the actual header, with exact capitalization. You may reorder columns, but may not add, omit, or duplicate them. Put verified records after the actual header. You may retain both instruction records unchanged, or output a clean CSV containing only the actual header and data rows; the app supports both. Do not change version, type, or base-currency markers, or embed the original ledger in the instruction section. The examples in these instructions are not user data.\n\nCommon Rules and Fields\n%@\n\nRules Specific to %@\n%@\n\nExample for This Type (Fictional; Understand Format Only, Do Not Import)\n%@\n\nOutput Requirements\nGenerate one downloadable \"%@\" CSV file under all rules above; retain every English column name. Each row must be one verified record of this type. Do not include titles, totals, subtotals, balances, duplicate displays, or Markdown fences. Do not turn scheduled rules into actual income/expense entries. Do not merge genuinely distinct transactions just because their amounts match.\nIf required values are missing; source files are unreadable; OCR text or dates are ambiguous; or currencies, exchange rates, transaction direction, interest settlement mode, or repayment method cannot be verified, ask the user first. Never guess, fabricate, fill missing values with zero, or silently drop rows. List uncertain items separately and do not include them in the CSV.\nGenerate a valid UUID for each new record and reuse existing IDs on subsequent conversions; preserve stable mappings for external transaction IDs. Reconcile totals or principal by currency. Separately report counts of original rows, output rows, excluded items, and unresolved items; do not place the report inside the CSV.\nThe app validates the complete CSV before previewing it and merges only after confirmation. Existing IDs are skipped without overwriting, and new IDs create new records. Importing does not create historical receipts; new recurring rules start paused. Do not alter the system fields in original-format data exports or force them into the simplified template. Use a native backup to restore complete historical state."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "给 AI：这是 FinTrack「%@」专用空白 CSV 模板（v1）。\n用户只需提供原始账本和本文件，无需另附格式说明或指令。原始账本可以是 Excel、CSV、PDF、照片、扫描件、文本或其他可读取资料；先识别明细，无法读取或有歧义时请向用户确认。\n只整理「%@」，不能混入其他三类数据。原表中的其他类型和无法确认的数据单独列为待处理清单，不能擅自改作本类型。\n当前账本本位币：%@。不得自行更换本位币、猜测币种或历史汇率。\n\n本文件结构\n第一条 CSV 记录以 #FinTrackTemplate 开头，依次保存版本、数据类型和本位币；第二条记录以 #AIInstructions 开头，其第二格就是本段说明。两条说明记录均不是财务数据，不能作为表头、交易或规则导入。第三条记录才是以下正式表头：\n%@\n正式表头的全部列必须保留，大小写一致，顺序可调，不得新增、遗漏或重复。请将确认的数据填写在正式表头之后。可原样保留这两条说明记录，也可输出只有正式表头和明细的干净 CSV，软件均支持；不得修改版本、类型、本位币标记，不要把原始账本嵌入说明区。说明中的示例也不是用户数据。\n\n通用规则与共用字段\n%@\n\n%@专有规则\n%@\n\n本类型示例（虚构，仅理解格式，不要导入）\n%@\n\n输出要求\n请按以上全部规则生成一个可下载的「%@」CSV文件；保留全部英文列名。一行一条确认的本类型记录，不加入标题、合计、小计、余额、重复展示或Markdown围栏。不要把规则再变成已发生收支，不擅自合并两条真实相同金额的记录。\n必填值缺失、原始资料无法读取、OCR文字或日期有歧义、币种/汇率/收支方向/计息或还款方式无法确认时，先问用户；不得猜测、编造、补0或静默丢行。待确认项单独列清单，不混入CSV。\n每条新记录生成有效UUID，重新转换时复用已有ID；外部流水号需保留稳定映射。按币种核对金额或本金合计，另行报告原始明细数、输出数、排除项及待确认项，报告不能混进CSV。\n软件先校验整文件再预览，确认后合并；相同ID跳过且不覆盖，新ID视为新记录。导入动作不会生成历史收据；新周期规则默认暂停。不要改动软件原格式数据导出的系统字段或把它套进简化模板，完整历史恢复使用原生备份。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
